{"key":"enterprise/T1620","id":"T1620","name":"Reflective Code Loading","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may reflectively load code into a process in order to conceal the execution of malicious payloads. Reflective loading involves allocating then executing payloads directly within the memory of the process, vice creating a thread or process backed by a file path on disk (e.g., Shared Modules). Reflectively loaded payloads may be compiled binaries, anonymous files (only present in RAM), or just snubs of fileless executable code (ex:…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1620","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--4933e63b-9b77-476e-ab29-761bc5b7d15a","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.630Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0021","name":"OS API Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0021","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9bde2f9d-a695-4344-bfac-f2dce13d121e","page":"telemetry/DC0021/"},{"id":"DC0035","name":"Process Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0035","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--1887a270-576a-4049-84de-ef746b2572d6","page":"telemetry/DC0035/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0029","name":"Script Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0029","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9f387817-df83-432a-b56b-a8fb7f71eedd","page":"telemetry/DC0029/"}],"strate